{"id":"chatcmpl-8c0ee3c1-62c5-46d7-a195-b9aaaef5a650","object":"chat.completion","created":1795249984,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a cross-validation strategy for medical image interpretation: query a domain-specific expert tool for a diagnostic claim, then independently verify the claim (including spatial laterality) using a grounded localization tool. The key insight is that laterality errors are common, so confirming the side via image coordinates (accounting for radiological L/R marker conventions) is essential before committing to an answer.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When a diagnostic question hinges on a spatial attribute (side, location), pair a semantic expert query with an independent localization/grounding tool to cross-check the spatial claim.\",\n    \"Use a targeted expert prompt that explicitly asks for the discriminating attribute (e.g., side and appearance) rather than a generic yes/no, to reduce ambiguity in the response.\",\n    \"Resolve laterality by mapping the grounded bounding box to image coordinates and reconciling with radiological marker conventions (patient right = image left), rather than trusting the expert's verbal label alone.\",\n    \"Require agreement between two independent evidence sources before finalizing an answer; treat concordance as the decision criterion and discordance as a signal to re-examine.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging QA\": \"Ask the expert tool for the specific finding plus its discriminating attribute (side, location, severity); then confirm with a grounded localization tool and check coordinate-to-anatomy mapping.\",\n    \"Spatial/laterality decisions\": \"Always verify left/right or positional claims against image coordinates and known orientation conventions; verbal labels alone are error-prone.\",\n    \"Multi-tool verification\": \"Design prompts so each tool provides complementary evidence (semantic diagnosis vs. spatial grounding), then require concordance before answering.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the expert's stated side matches the grounded bounding box location after applying image orientation conventions (e.g., radiological L marker).\",\n    \"Verify both tools independently support the same finding before selecting the final option.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":465,"total_tokens":877,"completion_tokens":412,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":465},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":412}}}